==Russian==
{{wikipedia|lang=ru}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ru|фоксал}}, {{l|ru|воксал}}, {{l|ru|воксгал}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|en|ru}} {{term|Vauxhall|lang=en}} (site of a pleasure garden and major railway station). The ending was influenced by {{term|зал||hall|lang=ru}}. The spelling {{term|фоксал|lang=ru}} attested in 1777 is from {{etyl|fr|-}} {{term|facs-hall|lang=fr}}, from the same English source.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Ru-вокзал.ogg|audio|lang=ru}}
* {{IPA|/vɐˈɡzal/|lang=ru}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun|вокза́л|m-in}}

# {{context|obsolete|lang=ru}} [[park]], [[pleasure garden]]
#* '''1813''', Aleksandr Pushkin, ‘To Natalie’
#*: ''На гуляньях иль в '''воксалах''' / Легким зефиром летал.''  At fetes and in parks, I've been flitting like a gentle zephyr.
# [[train station]], [[railroad station]], [[railway station]], [[depot]]

